{
  "0": {
    "Follow the Starlight.": "clips/cover-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "1": {
    "Ari knows three lights from their first journey. Dot finds one light that makes its own glow.": "clips/p01-narrator-story.m4a",
    "Ari, my scanner knows Venus, Mars and Jupiter. But one light is new. Look with me.": "clips/p01-dot-lead.m4a",
    "Jupiter is about 11 Earths wide.": "clips/p01-fact-03.m4a",
    "Mars looks red because its dust is rusty.": "clips/p01-fact-02.m4a",
    "Planets shine with sunlight. Stars make their own light.": "clips/p01-narrator-02.m4a",
    "Planets shine with the Sun's light. Stars make their own.": "clips/p01-fact-04.m4a",
    "Unknown light found. Mission accepted!": "clips/p01-dot-03.m4a",
    "Venus is the brightest planet in the night sky.": "clips/p01-fact-01.m4a",
    "Venus, Mars and Jupiter shine with borrowed sunlight.": "clips/p01-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "Which light is a star?": "clips/p01-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "10": {
    "Constellation stars can be very far apart in depth. From another viewpoint, their picture falls apart.": "clips/p10-narrator-story.m4a",
    "Dipper stars are about 80 to 125 light-years away.": "clips/p10-fact-01.m4a",
    "From Earth, different-depth stars line up as the familiar Dipper.": "clips/p10-narrator-02.m4a",
    "From another star the sky's pictures would look different.": "clips/p10-fact-04.m4a",
    "From the side the stars spread apart. Fly back to Earth's view.": "clips/p10-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "From where does the Dipper shape line up?": "clips/p10-narrator-01.m4a",
    "In about 100,000 years the Dipper will look different.": "clips/p10-fact-03.m4a",
    "Swing us round, Ari! From one spot only, the seven make the Dipper.": "clips/p10-dot-lead.m4a",
    "Their light left 80 to 125 years ago.": "clips/p10-fact-02.m4a",
    "They are neighbours in the sky, not in space.": "clips/p10-fact-05.m4a"
  },
  "11": {
    "A dense clump gives gravity enough material to begin making a star.": "clips/p11-narrator-02.m4a",
    "A glowing cloud of gas and dust is a nebula.": "clips/p11-fact-01.m4a",
    "A star-forming cloud is about 99 percent gas and 1 percent dust.": "clips/p11-fact-03.m4a",
    "A star-forming cloud is about minus 260 degrees Celsius.": "clips/p11-fact-02.m4a",
    "A thin cloud drifts apart. Gravity needs a dense clump to grip.": "clips/p11-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "Ari, sweep the cloud with your hand. Which clump is heavy enough for a star?": "clips/p11-dot-lead.m4a",
    "Stars begin in huge, cold clouds of gas and dust. Gravity gathers part of a cloud into a denser clump.": "clips/p11-narrator-story.m4a",
    "The Orion Nebula is a star nursery about 1,350 light-years away.": "clips/p11-fact-04.m4a",
    "The Sun was born in a cloud about 4.6 billion years ago.": "clips/p11-fact-05.m4a",
    "Which cloud can make a star?": "clips/p11-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "12": {
    "A Sun-like star takes tens of millions of years to form.": "clips/p12-fact-02.m4a",
    "A bicycle pump gets warm because compressing gas heats it.": "clips/p12-fact-03.m4a",
    "An unlit star is a protostar.": "clips/p12-fact-04.m4a",
    "Gravity pulls gas inward. The centre heats, and at about ten million degrees it ignites as a star.": "clips/p12-narrator-story.m4a",
    "Gravity squeezes the gas. Compression heats it until fusion begins.": "clips/p12-narrator-02.m4a",
    "More space lets the gas cool. Only squeezing warms it enough.": "clips/p12-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "Once lit, a star turns hydrogen into helium.": "clips/p12-fact-05.m4a",
    "Press and hold, Ari. Feel the middle warm up. What lights it?": "clips/p12-dot-lead.m4a",
    "The middle must reach about 10 million degrees Celsius.": "clips/p12-fact-01.m4a",
    "What makes the centre light?": "clips/p12-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "13": {
    "A red dwarf stays steady for trillions of years.": "clips/p13-fact-05.m4a",
    "Here is the Sun's whole life, Ari. Where does our today sit?": "clips/p13-dot-lead.m4a",
    "Our Sun is about 4.6 billion years into a roughly 10-billion-year stable stage.": "clips/p13-narrator-story.m4a",
    "The Sun is about 4.6 billion years old.": "clips/p13-fact-01.m4a",
    "The Sun is about halfway through its long, steady stage.": "clips/p13-narrator-02.m4a",
    "The Sun turns about 4 million tonnes of matter into energy every second.": "clips/p13-fact-03.m4a",
    "The Sun's brightness changes by about 0.1 percent in its 11-year cycle.": "clips/p13-fact-04.m4a",
    "The Sun's steady stage lasts about 10 billion years.": "clips/p13-fact-02.m4a",
    "The marker sits halfway along. Look between the start and the end.": "clips/p13-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "Where is the Sun now?": "clips/p13-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "14": {
    "Earth stays outside, and its story is not decided yet.": "clips/p14-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "Five billion years is about 16,000 times human history.": "clips/p14-fact-05.m4a",
    "In about 5 billion years the Sun swells into a red giant.": "clips/p14-fact-01.m4a",
    "Its surface will be about 3,000 degrees Celsius, so it looks red.": "clips/p14-fact-03.m4a",
    "Mercury and Venus are engulfed. Earth's fate is still uncertain.": "clips/p14-narrator-02.m4a",
    "Mercury and Venus will be swallowed.": "clips/p14-fact-04.m4a",
    "The red-giant Sun will be more than 100 times wider.": "clips/p14-fact-02.m4a",
    "Very far in the future, the Sun will become a red giant and expand beyond Mercury and Venus.": "clips/p14-narrator-story.m4a",
    "Watch the Sun swell, nice and slow, Ari. Which little worlds slip inside?": "clips/p14-dot-lead.m4a",
    "Which planets are swallowed by the red giant?": "clips/p14-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "15": {
