    "A Sun-like star releases its outer layers into a glowing ring and leaves an Earth-sized white dwarf.": "clips/p15-narrator-story.m4a",
    "A new white dwarf is over 100,000 degrees Celsius.": "clips/p15-fact-03.m4a",
    "A planetary nebula has nothing to do with planets.": "clips/p15-fact-01.m4a",
    "A white dwarf is about Earth-sized, roughly 12,700 kilometres wide.": "clips/p15-fact-02.m4a",
    "Not a black hole. Our kind of star leaves a small white dwarf.": "clips/p15-narrator-wrong.m4a",
    "The Ring Nebula is about 2,000 light-years away.": "clips/p15-fact-04.m4a",
    "The shell drifts away, Ari. Look at the middle. What is left?": "clips/p15-dot-lead.m4a",
    "The universe is 13.8 billion years old, and no white dwarf has gone dark.": "clips/p15-fact-05.m4a",
    "What remains after the outer gas drifts away?": "clips/p15-narrator-01.m4a"
  },
  "16": {
    "A red dwarf lives trillions of years.": "clips/p16-fact-03.m4a",
    "A star 10 times heavier lives tens of millions of years.": "clips/p16-fact-02.m4a",
